{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_gpu_plan", "label": "GPU plan (byte-identical CPU+GPU hybrid)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moved from GitHub issues #52-#57 into a doc because a plan nobody can find is not a plan; closing the issues was a filing decision, not a rejection."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_amdahl_ceiling_2_45x", "label": "Amdahl ceiling 2.45x (DP = 59.2% of CPU work)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L24", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Profile of 1M GIAB pairs -t8: matesw 39.2% + batched extension 20.0% go to GPU; 220.21s CPU falls to 89.8s if DP is free. Sort/dedup, seeding, SA, chaining stay on CPU."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_integrated_gpu_suffices", "label": "M4 Max integrated GPU suffices (~200-300 Gcell/s vs 33-116 needed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_dp_job_pure_function", "label": "DP job is a pure function (CPU/GPU split safe by construction)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Result depends only on (query, target, matrix, penalties, w, zdrop, h0), never on thread, order or ISA, so any job split or reordering leaves the SAM unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_no_floating_point", "label": "No floating point on GPU (int32, saturated u8, s16x2 only)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L81", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "half2 does not reproduce saturation at 255 nor exact ties."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_region_sort_stays_cpu", "label": "Region sort/dedup stays on CPU (ks_introsort permutation observable)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mem_sort_dedup_patch sorts on re only; pdqsort was verified to change the SAM md5."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_first_max_wins", "label": "Argmax tie rule: strict > (first maximum wins)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L224", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_issue_53_async_seam", "label": "#53 Async seam in SwBackend + batch-size measurement", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L121", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measure jobs per call first: >=4k jobs means one kernel launch per call; a few hundred means a cross-thread GPU queue and a changed SwBackend contract."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_swbackendasync", "label": "SwBackendAsync trait (submit / collect / queue_depth, BatchTicket)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L158", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "extend_batch becomes collect(submit(..)), keeping CPU backends and existing tests unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_bwa_gpu_crate", "label": "bwa-gpu crate (BWA4_GPU=metal|cuda|off, silent CPU fallback)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L181", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_issue_54_identity_gate", "label": "#54 GPU byte-identity gate (seven GPU traps)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L194", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written before the first kernel: a kernel right on 99.99% of jobs is wrong, 0.01% over 1M pairs breaks the md5. GPU-BWA-MEM claimed same results without published validation."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_saturation_i16_fallback", "label": "u8 saturation at 255 and i16 replay", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L228", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_n_target_12", "label": "N target encoded as 12 (N_TARGET, XOR substitution table)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L234", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_bwa4_gpu_split", "label": "BWA4_GPU_SPLIT gate (same md5 at 0.0..1.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L256", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_gpu_parity_sh", "label": "scripts/gpu_parity.sh (proposed, run three times)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L260", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three equal md5s guard against hardware non-determinism (uncorrected memory errors, driver reordering)."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_issue_55_metal_backend", "label": "#55 Metal backend (unified memory, zero copy)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L273", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First because the dev machine's integrated GPU already covers the full 2.45x and shared MTLBuffer removes PCIe copies. Port matesw single-row first, batched_extend after."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_one_thread_per_alignment", "label": "Inter-sequence layout: one thread per alignment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L310", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No cross-lane communication or reduction, so no identity risk; avoids GPU-BWA-MEM's warp-per-read wavefront which gave only 2x on SW."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_issue_56_cuda_backend", "label": "#56 CUDA backend (__vaddus4 saturated bytes, then DPX s16x2)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L341", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "__vaddus4/__vsubus4/__vmaxu4/__vcmpgtu4 are an exact transposition of the NEON u8 ops; DPX helps the i16 path only, after verifying ReLU clamp equivalence."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_issue_57_coscheduling", "label": "#57 CPU+GPU co-scheduling (static, adaptive, staggered pipeline)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L411", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Level 2 (EMA of observed throughput) probably suffices; level 3 needs a reorder buffer because SAM order is part of the byte-identity contract and raises RAM (#25)."}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_cudasw_4_0", "label": "CUDASW++4.0 (BMC Bioinformatics 2024)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L116", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11531700/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_gpu_bwa_mem", "label": "GPU-BWA-MEM (ICS 2023)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L115", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10425913/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gpu_plan_gasal2", "label": "GASAL2 (BMC Bioinformatics 2019)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/gpu-plan.md", "source_location": "L117", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6815017/", "captur